Package: scMarco
Type: Package
Title: Select marker gene combinations from binarized single-cell expression
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R:
    c(person("Yen-Chung", "Chen", email = "chenyenjung@gmail.com",
             role = c("aut", "cre")),
      person("Fred P.", "Davis", role = c("ctb", "cph"),
             comment = "author and copyright holder of the original mixture model code (opticlobe), adapted in R/mixture_fit.R and inst/stan/; see inst/COPYRIGHTS"))
Description: Helps choose combinations of marker genes, such as split-GAL4
    driver pairs, that label one cell type of a single-cell RNA-seq dataset
    and as few others as possible. Gene expression is binarized per cluster
    with a Bayesian mixture model, so that each gene is ON, OFF or ambiguous
    in each cluster and in each split of the data (stage, sex, species).
    scMarco ranks single genes and gene pairs by their off-target clusters,
    finds genes that tell apart a set of clusters, and plots co-expression,
    expression trends, UMAPs and the mixture-model fits, both from R and in an
    interactive Shiny app. Datasets are stored as AnnData (h5ad) files and
    can be built from Seurat objects.
